  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1100 AM MDT Thu Sep 24 2026\n\nAn upper-level high in eastern Texas and an upper-level trough in\nsouthern California will funnel additional monsoonal moisture \ninto our region today, bringing with it more showers and \nthunderstorms. Dona Ana County, Otero County, El Paso County, and \nHudspeth County are favored for thunderstorm development. Storms \nare expected to fire up in the Sacramento Mountains in the early \nafternoon hours, followed by a shortwave moving from the southwest\nfrom Chihuahua in the early evening. These regions are still \nunder a Flood Watch through late tonight, and up to an additional \ninch of rain on already saturated ground could lead to flooding \nconditions. The western edge of this wave will need to be closely \nexamined as the night progresses, as the most recent HRRR runs \nhave a band of heavy rainfall hitting Luna, Sierra, and western \nDona Ana County beginning around midnight.\n\nDrier air from Sonora and Arizona will enter southwestern New \nMexico by Friday afternoon, and PWATs are expected to trend down \nfrom 1.2\" to 1.0\". All the same, the 12Z HRRR has a few isolated \nshowers and thunderstorms in Hidalgo, Luna, and Grant Counties \npossible in the late afternoon hours, though I am skeptical if \nwestern New Mexico will see favorable conditions for thunderstorm \ndevelopment on Friday. The eastern reaches of our region will see \nmore favorable conditions for isolated-to-scattered thunderstorms \non Friday as moisture will be more plentiful there.\n\nSaturday and Sunday are both expected to be calm and warm as a \nridge hangs overhead. Then, subtropical moisture returns on late \nSunday night and will persist well into Tuesday. However, Monday \nis where the models begin to diverge in terms of how much moisture\nthe region will get, as well as if the region will see any \nimpacts from Polo; GFS is trending wetter, ECMWF is trending \ndrier. It is too soon to tell if Polo's remnants will impact the \nregion, but it is something we are watching closely.",
